 "description": "Whether a set of wallets on Base is one actor: who funded each with USDC, grouped by shared funder, with a verdict and the wallets it could not resolve. Turns \"55 distinct payers\" into \"one actor with 55 wallets\", or fails to.\nCall it on a line: a call without one has only a moment, enough for a small range of recent blocks, and is cut, uncharged, when it needs longer. from_block is a block number and defaults to the whole history; Base adds about 43,200 blocks a day. The first answer says how many windows the scan will take and about how many milliseconds, at the pace of recent scans, and each one after says how many are done.\n$0.000001 per millisecond on a line.\nPaid, on a line. With no wallet code, ZEAM :: Pass buys the time and opens the line for you, with a pass (https://mcp.zeamprism.com/pass) or your own wallet: https://mcp.zeamprism.com/how-to-pay\nExample: {\"addresses\":[\"0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD\",\"0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001\"],\"from_block\":51000000}",
 "inputSchema": {
  "examples": [
   {
    "addresses": [
     "0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD",
     "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001"
    ],
    "from_block": 51000000
   }
  ],
  "properties": {
   "addresses": {
    "description": "array \u2014 2 to 400 wallets, 0x form.",
    "items": {
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "from_block": {
    "description": "optional int \u2014 the block to start from; default the whole history. If the line runs out mid-scan you get what was scanned so far, marked partial; continue with to_block set to one below scanned.from.",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "line": {
    "description": "Optional. A line credential, for a client that cannot send the x-line header or _meta[\"zeam-pass/line\"]: the call runs on that line's time.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "to_block": {
    "description": "optional int \u2014 stop; default the head.",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "token": {
    "description": "optional string \u2014 the asset to follow, 0x form; default USDC.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "window": {
    "description": "optional int \u2014 blocks per snapshot, default 10000; smaller gives a short line its first snapshot sooner.",
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "addresses"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
